// result_end

\caption(Relative error of a float32 sum against the number of terms, both on log scales. Red: naive; orange: pairwise; blue: Kahan (hidden under the green line); green: double accumulator. Pale red and pale orange: the naive and pairwise worst-case bounds; grey: the typical naive error \(\sqrt n\,u\).)
\alttext(A log-log plot over log10 n from 1 to 7. The red naive curve rises from about minus 7.5 to about minus 4.2, close to and mostly just below the grey line of slope one half from minus 6.7 to minus 3.7. The pale red naive bound rises with slope 1 from minus 6.2 to 0. The orange, blue and green curves stay between minus 9 and minus 7 across the whole range, below the nearly flat pale orange pairwise bound at about minus 6.)

The naive error grows with \(n\), from \(3.8\times10^{-8}\) at \(n=10\) to \(6.7\times10^{-5}\) at \(10^7\). That is close to the grey \(\sqrt n\,u\) line, as the
random-sign model predicts, and a factor of about 20 000 inside the worst-case bound, which reaches 1.5 (no correct digits guaranteed) at \(n=10^7\).
Pairwise, Kahan and the wide accumulator do not grow at all. From \(n=10^4\) on they return the same float32 number, the exact sum
correctly rounded, so their error is just the final rounding, at most \(u/2\) relative. Pairwise is occasionally one rounding worse at small \(n\). The
naive error first exceeds the pairwise *bound* between \(n=10^3\) and \(10^4\), and at \(n=10^7\) it is about 1 700 times the pairwise error. `nn::sum` returns the
wide-accumulator value.

>> Fusion and determinism

The program times one pass of \(2x+0.5\) through `map_elements` against the composed `x * 2 + 0.5` and against a copy, on \(2^{24}\) float32 values
(64 MiB, larger than any cache). It then runs the same elementwise kernel with one and with eight threads, and sums the array naively in
\(k\) equal chunks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
using nn::Tensor;

int main() {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  nn::Generator gen(5);
  const std::int64_t n = 1 << 24;  // 16.8 million float32 values, 64 MiB
  const Tensor x = nn::uniform({n}, -1.0, 1.0, gen);
  auto median_seconds = [](auto&& body) {
    std::vector<double> t;
    for (int r = 0; r < 9; ++r) {
      const auto a = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
      body();
      t.push_back(std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - a).count());
    }
    std::ranges::sort(t);
    return t[t.size() / 2];
  };
  Tensor fused, composed;
  const double tf = median_seconds([&] { fused = nn::map_elements(x, [](auto v) { return v * 2.0f + 0.5f; }); });
  const double tc = median_seconds([&] { composed = x * 2.0 + 0.5; });
  const double copy = median_seconds([&] { (void)x.clone(); });
  const double mib = 1024.0 * 1024.0;
  std::print("| kernel | memory traffic (MiB) | median time (ms) | effective bandwidth (GiB/s) |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::print("| copy (clone) | {:.0f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |\n", 8.0 * n / mib, 1e3 * copy, 8.0 * n / copy / 1024 / mib);
  std::print("| fused ScaleShift (one pass) | {:.0f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |\n", 8.0 * n / mib, 1e3 * tf, 8.0 * n / tf / 1024 / mib);
  std::print("| x * 2 + 0.5 (two passes) | {:.0f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |\n", 16.0 * n / mib, 1e3 * tc, 16.0 * n / tc / 1024 / mib);
  std::print("\nFused against composed: {:.2f} times faster; results identical: {}\n", tc / tf,
             fused.to_vector<float>() == composed.to_vector<float>());

  // Determinism: elementwise kernels write each element once, so the thread count cannot matter.
  nn::set_num_threads(1);
  const auto one = nn::map_elements(x, [](auto v) { return std::exp(v) * v; }, 4096).to_vector<float>();
  nn::set_num_threads(8);
  const auto eight = nn::map_elements(x, [](auto v) { return std::exp(v) * v; }, 4096).to_vector<float>();
  nn::set_num_threads(0);
  std::print("- map_elements with 1 thread and with 8 threads: bit-identical = {}\n", one == eight);
  // A reduction split into k chunks, each summed naively and then combined, depends on k.
  const auto v = x.to_vector<float>();
  std::print("- naive float32 sum of all {} values, split into k equal chunks:\n\n| k | sum | difference from k = 1 (units of the last place) |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n", n);
  float base = 0;
  for (std::int64_t k : {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 64}) {
    float total = 0;
    for (std::int64_t c = 0; c < k; ++c) total += nn::sum_with(v.data() + c * (n / k), n / k, nn::Summation::Naive);
    if (k == 1) base = total;
    const float ulp = std::nextafter(std::abs(base), INFINITY) - std::abs(base);
    std::print("| {} | {:.4f} | {:+.0f} |\n", k, total, (total - base) / ulp);
  }
  double exact = 0;
  for (float e : v) exact += e;
  std::print("\nWide-accumulator sum: {:.4f}; nn::sum: {:.4f}; double sum: {:.4f}\n", nn::sum_with(v.data(), n, nn::Summation::WideAccumulator),
             nn::sum(x).item<float>(), exact);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| kernel | memory traffic (MiB) | median time (ms) | effective bandwidth (GiB/s) |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| copy (clone) | 128 | 14.3 | 8.8 |
| fused ScaleShift (one pass) | 128 | 15.2 | 8.2 |
| x * 2 + 0.5 (two passes) | 256 | 29.0 | 8.6 |

Fused against composed: 1.91 times faster; results identical: true
- map_elements with 1 thread and with 8 threads: bit-identical = true
- naive float32 sum of all 16777216 values, split into k equal chunks:

| k | sum | difference from k = 1 (units of the last place) |
| ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | -147.3252 | +0 |
| 2 | -147.3677 | -2786 |
| 4 | -147.4845 | -10442 |
| 8 | -147.4205 | -6246 |
| 16 | -147.3691 | -2877 |
| 64 | -147.3723 | -3087 |

Wide-accumulator sum: -147.3594; nn::sum: -147.3594; double sum: -147.3594
// result_end

The fused kernel moves 128 MiB at the speed of a copy, and the composed version moves 256 MiB at the same bandwidth, so it takes about twice
as long. As predicted, the arithmetic does not matter and the bytes do. The exact times vary from run to run. The bandwidth columns,
within a few per cent of each other, are the stable part. The two versions agree bit for bit here, because \(2x\) is exact in binary floating point.

The elementwise kernel gave bit-identical results with one and eight threads. The chunked naive sum did not: splitting the same \(2^{24}\) values
into 2 to 64 chunks moved the result by 2 786 to 10 442 units in the last place. No split gave back the \(k=1\) answer, and none is
"right": the exact value, \(-147.3594\), differs from all of them, by 0.008 to 0.13. The wide accumulator and `nn::sum` return it. A kernel
that splits a reduction by thread count therefore gives answers that depend on the machine. RowSums avoids this by giving whole rows to threads.

> A dataset: a fused logistic loss for breast-cancer diagnosis

The breast-cancer data (569 tumours, 30 standardised measurements of cell nuclei, 212 malignant) are fitted by ridge-penalised logistic regression,

$$
\min_{w,b}\;\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^n\Bigl[\log\bigl(1+e^{z_i}\bigr)-y_iz_i\Bigr]+\frac\lambda2\lVert w\rVert^2,\qquad z_i=x_i^\top w+b,\quad\lambda=0.01,
$$
\alttext(Minimise over w and b the mean over i of log of 1 plus e to the z i, minus y i z i, plus lambda over 2 times the squared norm of w, where z i equals x i transpose w plus b, and lambda is 0.01.)

by gradient descent with step \(1/L\). Here \(L\le\tfrac14(\lVert X^\top X\rVert_F/n+1)+\lambda\) bounds the curvature. The data term is computed once by `nn::sigmoid_cross_entropy`, composed from
library operations, and once by a fused kernel. Its forward is the stable \(\max(z,0)-zy+\log(1+e^{-\lvert z\rvert})\) summed in double, and its backward is
\((\sigma(z_i)-y_i)/n\), the derivative of the mean loss with respect to each logit, with \(\sigma\) evaluated without overflow as in the previous report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/custom_op_kernel_tapes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
using nn::Tensor;
using Tensors = std::vector<Tensor>;

// Fused mean binary cross-entropy with logits:
//   L = (1/n) sum_i [max(z_i, 0) - z_i y_i + log(1 + e^{-|z_i|})],   dL/dz_i = (sigmoid(z_i) - y_i) / n.
// One pass forward, one pass backward, no intermediates on the tape.
const nn::Function fused_bce(
    "FusedBCE",
    [](const Tensors& in) {
      const Tensor z = in[0].contiguous(), y = in[1].contiguous();
      if (z.shape() != y.shape()) throw std::invalid_argument("FusedBCE: logits and labels differ in shape");
      return nn::dispatch_floating(z.dtype(), "FusedBCE", [&](auto tag) {
        using T = decltype(tag);
        const T *zp = z.data_ptr<T>(), *yp = y.data_ptr<T>();
        double total = 0;
        for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < z.numel(); ++i)
          total += std::max<double>(zp[i], 0) - double(zp[i]) * yp[i] + std::log1p(std::exp(-std::abs(double(zp[i]))));
        return Tensors{nn::scalar(total / static_cast<double>(z.numel()), z.dtype())};
      });
    },
    [](const Tensors& in, const Tensors&, const Tensors& g) {
      const Tensor z = in[0].contiguous(), y = in[1].contiguous();
      const double scale = g[0].item() / static_cast<double>(z.numel());
      Tensor dz = nn::empty(z.shape(), z.dtype());
      nn::dispatch_floating(z.dtype(), "FusedBCE backward", [&](auto tag) {
        using T = decltype(tag);
        const T *zp = z.data_ptr<T>(), *yp = y.data_ptr<T>();
        T* out = dz.data_ptr<T>();
        for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < z.numel(); ++i) {
          const double e = std::exp(-std::abs(double(zp[i])));
          const double s = zp[i] >= 0 ? 1 / (1 + e) : e / (1 + e);
          out[i] = static_cast<T>((s - yp[i]) * scale);
        }
        return 0;
      });
      return Tensors{dz, Tensor()};  // labels get no gradient
    });

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto F64 = nn::DType::Float64;
  const auto cancer = dm::datasets::breast_cancer();
  const auto diagnosis = cancer.get_column<std::string>("diagnosis").values();
  const std::int64_t n = static_cast<std::int64_t>(diagnosis.size()), p = 30;
  std::vector<double> Z(static_cast<std::size_t>(n * p)), y(static_cast<std::size_t>(n));
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"mean_radius", "mean_texture", "mean_perimeter", "mean_area", "mean_smoothness", "mean_compactness", "mean_concavity", "mean_concave_points", "mean_symmetry", "mean_fractal_dimension", "radius_error", "texture_error", "perimeter_error", "area_error", "smoothness_error", "compactness_error", "concavity_error", "concave_points_error", "symmetry_error", "fractal_dimension_error", "worst_radius", "worst_texture", "worst_perimeter", "worst_area", "worst_smoothness", "worst_compactness", "worst_concavity", "worst_concave_points", "worst_symmetry", "worst_fractal_dimension"};
  for (std::int64_t j = 0; j < p; ++j) {
    const auto c = cancer.get_column<double>(names[j]).values();
    const double m = std::accumulate(c.begin(), c.end(), 0.0) / n;
    double ss = 0;
    for (double v : c) ss += (v - m) * (v - m);
    const double s = std::sqrt(ss / n);
    for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) Z[i * p + j] = (c[i] - m) / s;
  }
  for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) y[i] = diagnosis[i] == "malignant" ? 1.0 : 0.0;
  {
    std::ofstream out("build/cancer_standardised.csv");
    for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
      for (std::int64_t j = 0; j < p; ++j) out << std::format("{:.17g},", Z[i * p + j]);
      out << y[i] << "\n";
    }
  }
  const Tensor X = nn::from_vector(Z, {n, p}), Y = nn::from_vector(y, {n});
  const double lambda = 0.01;  // ridge penalty (lambda/2)||w||^2, intercept unpenalised
  // Smoothness constant: L <= max eigenvalue of [1 X]^T [1 X] / (4n) + lambda; 1/L is a safe step.
  const auto XtX = nn::matmul(nn::transpose(X), X).to_vector<double>();
  double frob = 0;
  for (double v : XtX) frob += v * v;
  const double step = 1.0 / (0.25 * (std::sqrt(frob) / n + 1.0) + lambda);

  auto train = [&](bool fused, int iters, nn::Tape* tape_out) {
    Tensor w = nn::zeros({p}, F64), b = nn::scalar(0.0, F64);
    for (int k = 0; k < iters; ++k) {
      auto wl = w.detach().requires_grad_(), bl = b.detach().requires_grad_();
      const Tensor z = nn::reshape(nn::matmul(X, nn::reshape(wl, {p, 1})), {n}) + bl;
      const Tensor data = fused ? fused_bce({z, Y})[0] : nn::sigmoid_cross_entropy(z, Y);
      const Tensor loss = data + 0.5 * lambda * nn::sum(nn::square(wl));
      if (tape_out && k == 0) *tape_out = nn::tape({loss}, {{wl, "w"}, {bl, "b"}});
      const auto g = nn::grad(loss, {wl, bl});
      w = (wl - step * g[0]).detach();
      b = (bl - step * g[1]).detach();
    }
    return std::pair{w, b};
  };
  nn::Tape tf, tc;
  (void)train(true, 1, &tf);
  (void)train(false, 1, &tc);
  std::print("Step size 1/L = {:.4f}. Ops on the tape of one loss evaluation: fused {}, composed {}.\n\n", step, tf.op_count(), tc.op_count());
  std::print("```\n{}```\n\n", tf.to_text());
  auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  fig.add(nn::plot_tape(tf, "Fused loss: one FusedBCE node"));
  fig.add(nn::plot_tape(tc, "Composed loss: sigmoid_cross_entropy"));
  fig.size(1100, 860).fit_panels();
  fig.save_svg("build/custom_op_kernel_tapes.svg");

  auto time_it = [&](bool fused) {
    const auto a = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
    auto r = train(fused, 3000, nullptr);
    return std::pair{r, std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - a).count()};
  };
  const auto [rf, sf] = time_it(true);
  const auto [rc, sc] = time_it(false);
  const auto wf = rf.first.to_vector<double>(), wc = rc.first.to_vector<double>();
  double diff = std::abs(rf.second.item() - rc.second.item());
  for (int j = 0; j < p; ++j) diff = std::max(diff, std::abs(wf[j] - wc[j]));
  // Optimality: gradient norm of the penalised loss at the fused solution.
  auto wl = rf.first.detach().requires_grad_(), bl = rf.second.detach().requires_grad_();
  const Tensor z = nn::reshape(nn::matmul(X, nn::reshape(wl, {p, 1})), {n}) + bl;
  const Tensor loss = fused_bce({z, Y})[0] + 0.5 * lambda * nn::sum(nn::square(wl));
  const auto g = nn::grad(loss, {wl, bl});
  double gn = g[1].item() * g[1].item();
  for (double v : g[0].to_vector<double>()) gn += v * v;
  int correct = 0;
  const auto zv = z.to_vector<double>();
  for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) correct += (zv[i] > 0) == (y[i] == 1.0);
  std::print("After 3000 gradient steps:\n\n");
  std::print("- penalised loss {:.6f}; gradient norm {:.1e}; training accuracy {}/{} = {:.3f}\n", loss.item(), std::sqrt(gn), correct, n, double(correct) / n);
  std::print("- largest difference between fused and composed coefficients: {:.1e}\n", diff);
  std::print("- time for 3000 steps: fused {:.0f} ms, composed {:.0f} ms\n\n", 1e3 * sf, 1e3 * sc);
  std::vector<std::pair<double, std::string>> top;
  for (int j = 0; j < p; ++j) top.push_back({wf[j], names[j]});
  std::ranges::sort(top, [](auto& a, auto& b) { return std::abs(a.first) > std::abs(b.first); });
  std::print("| feature (standardised) | coefficient |\n| :--- | ---: |\n| intercept | {:.4f} |\n", rf.second.item());
  for (int j = 0; j < 6; ++j) std::print("| {} | {:.4f} |\n", top[j].second, top[j].first);
}
```
